  "operation": {
    "kind": "prompt",
    "user": "Build the composite, and say honestly what it dropped.\n\n## The criteria\n\n{{.inputs.criteria}}\n\n## The candidates\n\n{{.inputs.candidates}}\n\n## The scores\n\n{{.inputs.scores}}\n\n## What to produce\n\n`composite` — a candidate built from the best of the others, in the same shape\nas they are. Take each candidate's `unique` seriously: the composite exists to\nkeep what would otherwise be lost. **Say what it dropped and why** — a composite\nthat claims to keep everything has kept nothing that conflicted, which means it\nhas not chosen.\n\n`composite_score` — the composite scored against the same criteria, by the same\nmethod. Do not flatter it. A composite that grafts three stances together\nusually loses on coherence, and that is exactly what the arithmetic in `verdict`\nis for.\n\n`residue` — **one or two lines**, in the form the phase's doc actually carries.\nThis is the only part of the exploration that survives into `docs/`; the\ncandidates and the scoring table stay on the task.\n\n| Kind | Where the residue lands |\n| --- | --- |\n| `product` | **Framings considered** — the rejected reading, and why not |\n| `ux` | The flow's **Where this fits**, or a new pattern if the shape recurs |\n| `ui` | **Instead consider** on the component |\n| `engineering` | A numbered **decision record** — the one place a losing option keeps its full argument |\n| anything else | One line on the doc this phase produced |\n\nThis exploration is kind `{{.inputs.candidate_kind}}`.\n\nThe test for the residue: a month from now nobody reads the scoring table, and\nsomebody will re-propose the losing option. Write the line that answers them.\nIf a losing candidate is worth more than a row, it was a decision, and it gets a\ndecision record.\n\n`exploration_doc` — the brief, the criteria, the candidates and the scores, as\none markdown document. This is a run artifact on the task, not a file in\n`docs/`.\n",
    "config": {
      "model": "claude-opus-5"
    },
    "input": {},
    "output": {
      "name": "output",
      "kind": "json",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
